recommend check-in (Keaton) the integration is a gate, not a lap: two piers hold six different reds under %233, %234, and %235, and twelve rows %236-%247 exist only here. REDS %230 named this question OPEN and this is its second firing, now across a rewritten history. %230's rule gives the answer -- earlier stamp keeps the number, so this pier holds %233-%235 and the bench's shift to %248-%250 -- and applying it means renumbering another pier's ledger and carrying three commits across a 5,092-file season-to-chapter molt. The package waits whole on refs/heads/pier/one-tree-one-number, every guard green. Agent-doable on this pier meanwhile: the twelve gated xargs sites want one shared portable helper, which is one edit repairing every caller and every caller yet written.
